{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Before it was in the earth.</b> Every טֶרֶם in Scripture means 'before not yet' — it is not a term of 'prior to', and it is not a verb to say הִטְרִים as one would say הִקְדִים, and this proves it. And further: ״כִּי טֶרֶם תִּירְאוּן״ (Exodus 9) — 'you do not yet fear.' And so this too, explain: 'it was not yet in the earth' — when the creation of the world was completed on the sixth day, before man was created. And ״וְכָל עֵשֶׂב הַשָּׂדֶה טֶרֶם יִצְמַח״ — 'had not yet sprouted.' And in the three instances where it says ״תּוֹצֵא הָאָרֶץ״ — they did not emerge, but stood at the mouth of the ground until the sixth day." "<b>For it had not rained.</b> And why had it not rained? Because man was not there to work the ground, and there was no one to recognize the goodness of the rains. And when man came and knew that they are a need of the world, he prayed for them, and they fell, and the trees and the vegetation sprouted." "<b>YHWH Elohim.</b> YHWH is His name; Elohim — that He is Ruler and Judge over all. And so the meaning of this everywhere, according to its plain sense: YHWH — He is Elohim."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:15.416236075Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}